{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524198-psychics-vs-sorcerer","id":1524198,"title":"Psychics vs Sorcerer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-17T09:42:40-07:00","id":1524198,"title":"Psychics vs Sorcerer","content":"Hi. <br /> <br /> Mages are too powerful for my purposes. I prefer working with the Sorcerers and Psychics in the WoD, but I'm not sure what the difference is between the two regarding feats. What are the pros and cons of playing one or the other? Is it that Psychic feats are more immediate, but Sorcerer feats are more long-range? Help me out here!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26676-squiggles","name":"Squiggles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-17T12:40:55-07:00","id":1524205,"title":"","content":"Psychic powers tend to be specific and binary (either they go off with one role, or they don't). This makes them better for on the spot powers, but lacking in versatility or ways to build up effects if they need to push past their current limits.<br /> <br /> Sorcery powers tend to be broader, and with more gradation in terms of what they can do and how well you do. This makes them better for ritual powers that can cover a lot of bases, and get boosted with more resources, but less capable of using anything that's not prepped ahead of time on short notice.<br /> <br /> There's also a setting conceit where psychic powers are frequently more &quot;wild&quot; and finding teachers or groups that understand and can train psychics is harder, while sorcerers tend to have much longer standard organizations to join and gain access to training and support. This is not inherently necessary to how their rules function, but is a consideration (and it does stem from how they tend to operate).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T01:33:51-07:00","id":1524218,"title":"","content":"Another difference is one of &quot;Feel&quot;.<br /> <br /> Psychics tend to just require the power of their minds to cast Effects. For this reason, the power itself is far more centered in the character, and what they use it for. So you're allowed to run a &quot;generic Psychic&quot;, in the sense it could be anyone and have most any power.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers, much like Mages, are deeply reliant on a pre-defined Focus (Paradigm, Practice, and Instruments). The act of doing Sorcery requires the props and trappings relevant to the Sorcerer's magical style. This might be Witchcraft, Hermetic High Ritual, Weird Science, Martial Arts, etc. HOW the Sorcerer performs the Effects is as much, if not more important, than what Effects they do. There is no &quot;generic Sorcerer&quot;. You have to define what <i>kind</i> of Sorcerer they are. This provides more opportunities for creating memorable NPCs, but also demands another layer of work to flesh them out. Figuring out how not only the Paths they know and their backgrounds, but how those backgrounds intersect with and inform/are informed by their magical style.<br /> <br /> Being a Psychic or Sorcerer implies different things about how the character acquired their powers. Psychics get away more readily with just having been a natural talent. They might have their abilities unlocked somehow, but it's very easily to say they were just born with it. A Sorcerer, meanwhile, must almost always learn their magic externally. Whether this is through personal research, reading old books, having a Mentor, or being initiated in a Sorcerer organization, group, or society. Either mode implies a great deal about the character and what their deal is, which must be considered when designing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T11:47:39-07:00","id":1524283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524198-psychics-vs-sorcerer?p=1524218#post1524218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another difference is one of &quot;Feel&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 100% agree. But is there anything beyond feel that is a pro or con for either? Like in game terms do you view them being able to do something the other can't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26676-squiggles","name":"Squiggles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T13:50:36-07:00","id":1524286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squiggles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524198-psychics-vs-sorcerer?p=1524283#post1524283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 100% agree. But is there anything beyond feel that is a pro or con for either? Like in game terms do you view them being able to do something the other can't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> already mentioned it, but sorcery is more versatile. Aspects allow you to tweak a Path effect to your needs. You can use teamwork to cast stronger spells. You can use Rituals (which is probably the most significant difference between the two imo). The downside is, it's complicated and increasingly difficult to cast. Focus might get in the way of teamwork. If you play by default rules, spells may take several rounds to cast.<br /> <br /> Psychic Phenomena are less complex, but also less versatile. On the upside, they don't care about Witnesses and scale gradually in both power and difficulty. Focus isn't a concern, what counts is just Willpower. Effects are almost always instant.<br /> <br /> It didn't come up for me yet, but if I had a psychic player in my group I would probably have a good look at importing psionic rules from Trinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T15:34:34-07:00","id":1524292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524198-psychics-vs-sorcerer?p=1524286#post1524286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It didn't come up for me yet, but if I had a psychic player in my group I would probably have a good look at importing psionic rules from Trinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, as Sorcerer Revised points out in a text box, the psychic powers found in WoD operate on a different scale of power than those found in Trinity. Trinity's psionics are far greater and more overt. It's a setting where psionics are a known and familiar background element.<br /> <br /> Psychic powers in World of Darkness, at least available to Psychics, are &quot;lower to the ground&quot;, often more subtle. They're meant to be more mysterious, even unreliable. As befits as setting where the supernatural exists in the shadows, and where their influence is just as obscure. The powers available to a WoD Psychic tend towards the uncanny.<br /> <br /> It matters a great deal what tone and power level you're going for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T16:08:20-07:00","id":1524294,"title":"","content":"Oh, I agree with that. The import wouldn't be so much the powers themselves and more from the framework around them. Thing is, in both Sorcerer 20th and Revised, Psychic Phenomena get about two paragraphs of text if you exclude the descriptions of the powers themselves. For a player character I would want to offer something with a little more depth to it, and Trinity seems the the natural pick to look at. Granted, it's been a while since I played it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T16:44:44-07:00","id":1524295,"title":"","content":"By the way, Sorcerers in the WoD often work to develop psychic powers. Most sorcery is slow and obvious were psychic powers are relatively quick and hard to detect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T00:37:17-07:00","id":1524312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524198-psychics-vs-sorcerer?p=1524286#post1524286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It didn't come up for me yet, but if I had a psychic player in my group I would probably have a good look at importing psionic rules from Trinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for mentioning Trinity. It just doesn't make sense to me that if a Sorcerer or Psychic Awaken, they would likely become a Mage. It makes sense for Sorcerers, but I would imagine Psychics would Awaken to be something else. For a long time, I toyed with them Awakening to being Changelings for various reasons, but Awakening to be Trinity Psions may be even better.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26676-squiggles","name":"Squiggles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T02:05:20-07:00","id":1524313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squiggles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524198-psychics-vs-sorcerer?p=1524312#post1524312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for mentioning Trinity. It just doesn't make sense to me that if a Sorcerer or Psychic Awaken, they would likely become a Mage. It makes sense for Sorcerers, but I would imagine Psychics would Awaken to be something else. For a long time, I toyed with them Awakening to being Changelings for various reasons, but Awakening to be Trinity Psions may be even better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember &quot;Psionics&quot; is a Mage paradigm. Plenty of Mages see themselves as powerful Psions.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is slower and more obvious but that allows for greater flexibility and manipulation of the process. Psychic powers are quicker and more covert, but at the cost of a great deal of complexity and the opportunities that allows. It's not an either/or, it's a what works here.<br /> <br /> If I want to tell the Storm Troopers &quot;These aren't the Droids you're looking for.&quot; I would use psychic power. If I want to make the house I live in psychicly invisible, by constantly putting out the thought &quot;This house is to dull and worthless for you to notice.&quot; That's a complex group of sorcery rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 10-20-2023, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T03:35:50-07:00","id":1524314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524198-psychics-vs-sorcerer?p=1524313#post1524313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember &quot;Psionics&quot; is a Mage paradigm. Plenty of Mages see themselves as powerful Psions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but Psionics as a possible evolution of Psychic powers is something mechanically distinct. Awakening is a very Mage thing that I would keep separate, because a slumbering Avatar isn't really tied to any specific type of Numen. When the Avatar of a Psychic wakes, they are becoming a Mage and their Focus will likely be that of a 'Psion'. If I understood <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26676-squiggles\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26676_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26676\" data-vbnamecard=\"26676\">Squiggles</a> right, they were talking about the next step up for Psychics that does not involve an Avatar.<br /> <br /> If I recall correctly, the term Trinity uses for a Psion unlocking their powers naturally (without a Prometheus Chamber) is Eruption, although more commonly used for Novas. I would probably stick with that to make the distinction. Obviously, Mage and Trinity weren't really meant to be smushed together like that. I would really have to read up on current Trinity to see how compatible it would be. Sorcerer Revised at least encourages to check the Player's Guide for advanced rules in the text box <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> mentioned, but I'm not sure what the referenced edition would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 10-20-2023, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T06:07:51-07:00","id":1524317,"title":"","content":"\u201cEruption\u201d is never used for psions; it's specific to Novas. Even if you insist on psychics Awakening as something other than mages, I'd still use the term \u201cAwakening\u201d for it. <br /> <br /> I'd also aim less for psions than for psiads (those being the ones who Awaken without Prometheus Chambers, but who also don't have the \u201csingle Aptitude\u201d restriction that psions have); and depending on which edition you use, I'd either use the Freeform Techniques from the first edition's <b>Trinity Player's Guide</b> (starting on page 161) or the Aptitude Shaping from the more recent edition's <b>Prometheus Unbound</b> (starting on page 162). <br /> <br /> The advantage of going with the first edition is that the underlying game engine is more similar to <b>Mage</b>, making the work needed to make the two compatible a bit less. <br /> <br /> Finally, you could make psions (as opposed to psiads) a Technocratic or Etherite thing: there's a Tasty Bit for Trinity<b> Continuum: Aeon</b> called <b>The Phoebe Trust</b> which details a 20th and 21st century organization that has developed some imperfect ways to unlock a psion's potential and Awaken him or her, at a cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T08:34:49-07:00","id":1524324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524198-psychics-vs-sorcerer?p=1524292#post1524292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, as Sorcerer Revised points out in a text box, the psychic powers found in WoD operate on a different scale of power than those found in Trinity. Trinity's psionics are far greater and more overt. It's a setting where psionics are a known and familiar background element.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Trinity/TC:\u00c6on are more in the vein of sci fi superheroes like certain aspects of the X-Men or various anime. WoD psychics are patterned after early Stephen King material (Carrie, The Shining, The Dead Zone, Firestarter) and films like Scanners.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T09:09:28-07:00","id":1524326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524198-psychics-vs-sorcerer?p=1524317#post1524317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cEruption\u201d is never used for psions; it's specific to Novas. Even if you insist on psychics Awakening as something other than mages, I'd still use the term \u201cAwakening\u201d for it.<br /> <br /> I'd also aim less for psions than for psiads (those being the ones who Awaken without Prometheus Chambers, but who also don't have the \u201csingle Aptitude\u201d restriction that psions have); and depending on which edition you use, I'd either use the Freeform Techniques from the first edition's <b>Trinity Player's Guide</b> (starting on page 161) or the Aptitude Shaping from the more recent edition's <b>Prometheus Unbound</b> (starting on page 162).<br /> <br /> The advantage of going with the first edition is that the underlying game engine is more similar to <b>Mage</b>, making the work needed to make the two compatible a bit less.<br /> <br /> Finally, you could make psions (as opposed to psiads) a Technocratic or Etherite thing: there's a Tasty Bit for Trinity<b> Continuum: Aeon</b> called <b>The Phoebe Trust</b> which details a 20th and 21st century organization that has developed some imperfect ways to unlock a psion's potential and Awaken him or her, at a cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification, correction, and pointers. I apparently misremembered the Eruption bit, and I don't think I have heard about psiads before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T13:50:04-07:00","id":1524338,"title":"","content":"Still, if we want Trinity style Psionics in a WoD game, it would be a homebrew (but aren't they all), we could use the term eruption. I think I'd prefer the term &quot;Emergence.&quot; It's the same term they use to describe a butterfly leaving its chrysalis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T13:03:56-07:00","id":1524363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524198-psychics-vs-sorcerer?p=1524313#post1524313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember &quot;Psionics&quot; is a Mage paradigm. Plenty of Mages see themselves as powerful Psions.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is slower and more obvious but that allows for greater flexibility and manipulation of the process. Psychic powers are quicker and more covert, but at the cost of a great deal of complexity and the opportunities that allows. It's not an either/or, it's a what works here.<br /> <br /> If I want to tell the Storm Troopers &quot;These aren't the Droids you're looking for.&quot; I would use psychic power. If I want to make the house I live in psychicly invisible, by constantly putting out the thought &quot;This house is to dull and worthless for you to notice.&quot; That's a complex group of sorcery rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an excellent visual and analogy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524198-psychics-vs-sorcerer?p=1524324#post1524324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. Trinity/TC:\u00c6on are more in the vein of sci fi superheroes like certain aspects of the X-Men or various anime. WoD psychics are patterned after early Stephen King material (Carrie, The Shining, The Dead Zone, Firestarter) and films like Scanners.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never noticed but now I can't unnotice it! Thanks for pointing that out.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26676-squiggles","name":"Squiggles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-25T16:21:29-07:00","id":1524510,"title":"","content":"I tend to view psychic-powers as inherent-talent whereas sorcery is learned-skill through belief in magic. I go by the rule that one psychic-power, costs seven freebie-points and a second psychic-power costs fourteen freebie-points, thereby using up all your starting mortal-freebies. Sorcery can be bought at character-creation and other, &quot;Spells', can be purchased with Experience-Points in the future.<br /> <br /> Also, in <i>Cyberpunk 2020's Night's Edge</i>: magic-spells are rituals that are just pscionic-powers, but are more difficult to cast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":2521,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","user":"Iguazu","date":".  Addum 10-25-2023, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T17:19:54-07:00","id":1524557,"title":"","content":"Note also that in the recent Sorcerer books (Sorcerer: Paths of Power and M20 Sorcerer), Paths use Attribute+Ability dice pools while psychic phenomena use Willpower dice pools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T10:11:19-08:00","id":1525849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524198-psychics-vs-sorcerer?p=1524510#post1524510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to view psychic-powers as inherent-talent whereas sorcery is learned-skill through belief in magic. I go by the rule that one psychic-power, costs seven freebie-points and a second psychic-power costs fourteen freebie-points, thereby using up all your starting mortal-freebies. Sorcery can be bought at character-creation and other, &quot;Spells', can be purchased with Experience-Points in the future.<br /> <br /> Also, in <i>Cyberpunk 2020's Night's Edge</i>: magic-spells are rituals that are just pscionic-powers, but are more difficult to cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>They, actually are supposed to be inherent. In fact, being born with a disability increase your chance of being a psychic. To 2 percent if I am not mistaken, but could be wrong. I think disability in this context essentially means being born with a physical flaw. <br /> This was in the old pentex book, or something along those lines<br /> Not sure if it can also be learned by rote","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T11:16:08-08:00","id":1525853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1524198-psychics-vs-sorcerer?p=1525849#post1525849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They, actually are supposed to be inherent. In fact, being born with a disability increase your chance of being a psychic. To 2 percent if I am not mistaken, but could be wrong. I think disability in this context essentially means being born with a physical flaw.<br /> This was in the old pentex book, or something along those lines<br /> Not sure if it can also be learned by rote</div> </div> </div> </div>You do have a point, game-mechanics-wise; you get psychic-powers you need to get a lot of flaws to get extra freebie-points, though, the 21-points should be enough, but, it's never enough: In Night's Edge, skills aren't one to one regarding psychic-powers; to get a psychic-power at an average use level of five, you to spend 25 skill-points ( you only get 40 at character-creation). So, you'll get a character that can read minds, but can't fire a gun or do much else. <br /> <br /> And I agree that psychic-powers are inherent. Magic, is a belief, like True Faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T20:44:13-08:00","id":1525992,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't call magic (without the Special K) a belief; I'd call it an awareness, an understanding, or an attunement. Sorcery works because reality is <i>not </i>wholly Scientific, and the sorcerer has some knowledge of and/or connection to a part of it that's supernatural. Sorcery is definitely not inherent, the way psychic phenomena are; but it's more knowledge-based than belief-based.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}